# A program given no input at all. There is no `.in` beside this case, which
# is how the runner says so; at a command line it is `vine prog.vine` with
# nothing redirected in, and at the REPL it is every time, because there
# standard input is where the program itself is arriving from.
#
# The refusal rather than a wait is the decision: read() wants all of standard
# input, so waiting at a terminal means sitting silently until Ctrl-D, which
# looks like a frozen report. See **Reading** in docs/spec.md.
let text = read()
print(len(text))
